    <bpmn:process id="W_W1457" name="W1457. RFID-Based Smart Shelf Inventory Monitoring &amp; Automated Replenishment Trigger PoC" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or Category Manager identifies high-value category with chronic stockout issues
Frequency: PoC planning: quarterly; PoC execution: 3–6 month pilot; post-PoC evaluation: at pilot completion
Volume: PoC scope: 1 flagship store, power tools category (~1,750 SKUs, unit value PHP 3,000–25,000)
Owner: IT Innovation Lead
Participants: IT Innovation Lead, Store Manager (pilot store), Category Manager (power tools), RFID Vendor, CIO, Finance (CAPEX)
Source: workflow W1457 — RFID-Based Smart Shelf Inventory Monitoring &amp; Automated Replenishment Trigger PoC</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1457_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1457_Lane1" name="IT Innovation Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1457_Lane2" name="RFID Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1457_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1457_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1457_Start5" name="Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or Category Manager identifies high-value…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1457_Task6" name="PoC planning &amp; vendor selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PoC planning &amp; vendor selection: Select pilot store (highest power tools shrinkage in Metro Manila); evaluate 3 RFID vendors on read accuracy in metal-heavy retail, Philippine experience, ERP integration, cost per tag (target ≤ PHP 15); define success criteria: inventory accuracy ≥ 99%, theft detection improvement ≥ 30%
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1457_Task7" name="Infrastructure installation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Infrastructure installation: RFID vendor installs smart shelf antennas on 8 shelving units, backroom portal reader, handheld reader, and middleware server; tag all existing power tools inventory (~1,500 units)
Responsible (R): RFID Vendor / IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1457_Task8" name="Baseline measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Baseline measurement: Wall-to-wall physical count of power tools; record stockout rate, replenishment lead time, shrinkage rate, and cycle counting labor hours
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1457_Task9" name="PoC execution (3–6 months)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PoC execution (3–6 months): Smart shelves continuously read tags; auto-generate replenishment alerts to Stock Associate handheld; detect potential theft (item leaves shelf without POS transaction); flag misplaced items; weekly accuracy review vs. baseline
Responsible (R): System / IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1457_Task10" name="Post-PoC evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-PoC evaluation: Compile results: accuracy improvement, stockout reduction, shrinkage reduction, labor savings, false positive rate on theft alerts; calculate ROI; recommend expand/extend/discontinue
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1457_Task11" name="Scale-up planning (if approved)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Scale-up planning (if approved): Phased rollout to top 20 high-shrinkage stores, then all stores; negotiate volume pricing (tag target ≤ PHP 8); integrate with replenishment engine per W4; CAPEX per W21
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / CIO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1457_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1457_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1457_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1457_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-331 (ensure controlled execution — Emerging Technology &amp; PoC (PA-30.1).) | - operational: IT Innovation Lead review and approval gate
Owner: IT Innovation Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1457_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1457_Annotation13" targetRef="W1457_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
