    <bpmn:process id="W_W1458" name="W1458. Autonomous Mobile Robot (AMR) Goods-to-Person Picking PoC for DC Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or DC Manager identifies pick productivity bottleneck during peak season
Frequency: PoC planning: quarterly; PoC execution: 3–6 month pilot; post-PoC evaluation: at completion
Volume: PoC scope: DC3 (South Luzon Hub, 40,000 sqm); pilot zone: 1 aisle of tiles/plumbing SKUs (~800 SKUs)
Owner: IT Innovation Lead
Participants: IT Innovation Lead, DC Manager (DC3), AMR Vendor, CIO, VP Supply Chain, Finance (CAPEX)
Source: workflow W1458 — Autonomous Mobile Robot (AMR) Goods-to-Person Picking PoC for DC Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1458_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1458_Lane1" name="IT Innovation Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1458_Lane2" name="AMR Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1458_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1458_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1458_Start5" name="Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or DC Manager identifies pick productivity…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1458_Task6" name="PoC planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PoC planning: Define pilot zone (~500 sqm, 800 SKUs); evaluate 3 AMR vendors (Geek+, HAI Robotics, Locus) on navigation, payload (tiles weigh 20–30 kg — AMR must handle 50 kg+), pick station ergonomics, WMS integration, Philippine support, unit cost (PHP 500K–1.5M each); success criteria: pick productivity ≥ +50%, walking reduction ≥ 70%, accuracy ≥ 99.5%, ROI payback ≤ 3 years
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1458_Task7" name="Pilot zone setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pilot zone setup: Deploy 3–5 AMR units in pilot aisle; install pick station; map existing layout into AMR fleet software (no infrastructure changes); integrate with WMS; train 3 DC Stock Associates as pick station operators
Responsible (R): AMR Vendor / DC Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1458_Task8" name="Baseline measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Baseline measurement: Measure current RF-directed picking: units/labor hour, pick cycle time, walking distance/shift, pick accuracy for pilot zone SKUs
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / DC Ops Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1458_Task9" name="PoC execution (3–6 months)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PoC execution (3–6 months): AMR transports shelf pods to pick station; operator scans/packs items per WMS instructions; AMR returns pod and retrieves next; system measures units/hour, utilization, queue time, accuracy, uptime; weekly metrics review
Responsible (R): System / DC Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1458_Task10" name="Post-PoC evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-PoC evaluation: Compile results: productivity vs. baseline, AMR uptime, operator satisfaction; calculate full DC ROI (20–30 units × PHP 500K–1.5M = PHP 15M–60M/DC); recommend expand/extend/discontinue
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1458_Task11" name="Scale-up (if approved)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Scale-up (if approved): Phased rollout to DC3, DC1/DC2, DC4; labor redeployment plan for displaced pickers; CAPEX per W21
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1458_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1458_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1458_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1458_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-331 (ensure controlled execution — Emerging Technology &amp; PoC (PA-30.1).) | - operational: IT Innovation Lead review and approval gate
Owner: IT Innovation Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
