    <bpmn:process id="W_W1569" name="W1569. Computer Vision-Based Shelf Gap Detection, Planogram Compliance Monitoring &amp; Automated Replenishment Alerting PoC" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or persistent stockout issue identified in store analytics per W1567; or vendor co-innovation proposal
Frequency: PoC planning: quarterly; PoC execution: 3-month pilot; post-PoC evaluation: at completion
Volume: PoC scope: 5 pilot stores (mix of Metro Manila and provincial); coverage: power tools and hardware fastener aisles (~500 SKUs per store)
Owner: IT Innovation Lead
Participants: IT Innovation Lead, Computer Vision Vendor, Store Manager (pilot stores), Department Supervisor, Category Manager (Tools/Hardware), COO
Source: workflow W1569 — Computer Vision-Based Shelf Gap Detection, Planogram Compliance Monitoring &amp; Automated Replenishment Alerting PoC</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1569_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1569_Lane1" name="IT Innovation Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1569_Lane2" name="Computer Vision Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1569_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1569_Start4" name="Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or persistent stockout issue identified in…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1569_Task5" name="PoC planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PoC planning: Define pilot scope and success criteria: (a) pilot stores: 5 stores (2 Metro Manila, 1 Cebu, 1 Davao, 1 North Luzon — mix of store sizes and lighting conditions); (b) pilot aisles: power tools section (high-value items, manageable SKU count ~150) and hardware fastener wall (high-SKU density, small items ~350 SKUs); (c) technology options: (i) retrofit existing CCTV cameras with computer vision software (lower cost, lower image quality for shelf-level detail), (ii) dedicated shelf-facing cameras per aisle (higher cost, higher accuracy); (d) success criteria: (i) shelf gap detection accuracy ≥ 90% (verified by manual audit), (ii) planogram compliance detection accuracy ≥ 85%, (iii) alert-to-replenishment time reduction ≥ 50% vs. current manual process, (iv) estimated ROI payback ≤ 2 years for chain-wide rollout
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1569_Task6" name="Pilot deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pilot deployment: (a) install dedicated shelf-facing cameras in pilot aisles at 5 stores (4 cameras per aisle, 2 aisles per store = 40 cameras total); (b) vendor trains computer vision model on BuildRight product images from VS-137 PIM (W252 item master / W298 attribute templates): (i) upload product images per SKU (front-facing packaging), (ii) map planogram for each pilot aisle: product ID → shelf position (bay, shelf, position), (iii) model learns to identify each product and detect gaps; (c) integrate alert system with Stock Associate handheld devices (push notification: &quot;Gap detected: Power Drill SKU 12345, Bay 3, Shelf 2, Position 5 — replenish from backroom&quot;)
Responsible (R): Computer Vision Vendor / IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 3–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1569_Task7" name="Baseline measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Baseline measurement: Before activating alerts: (a) measure current shelf gap frequency: manual audit every 4 hours for 2 weeks in pilot aisles — record gap count, gap duration (time from gap appearance to replenishment); (b) measure planogram compliance: manual audit comparing shelf layout to planogram; (c) establish baseline metrics for comparison
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1569_Task8" name="PoC execution (3 months)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PoC execution (3 months): (a) computer vision system runs continuously during store hours: (i) cameras capture shelf images every 15 minutes, (ii) model detects gaps and planogram violations, (iii) alerts pushed to Stock Associate devices; (b) weekly metrics review: (i) gap detection rate (CV-detected gaps ÷ manually verified gaps), (ii) false positive rate (CV-detected gaps that are not actual gaps — e.g., product packaging variation mistaken for gap), (iii) average gap duration (CV-assisted vs. baseline), (iv) Stock Associate feedback on alert usefulness
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / System
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1569_Task9" name="Post-PoC evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-PoC evaluation: Compile results: (a) accuracy metrics vs. success criteria; (b) gap duration reduction (target: 50%+); (c) estimated lost sales recovery (gap duration reduction × average hourly sales per SKU); (d) chain-wide rollout cost: 200 stores × 2 aisles × 4 cameras × PHP 5–10K/camera = PHP 8–16M + software licensing PHP 3–5M/year; (e) ROI: estimated lost sales recovery ÷ annual cost; (f) recommend: expand to more aisles/stores, modify technology approach, or discontinue
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1569_Task10" name="Scale-up (if approved)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Scale-up (if approved): Phased rollout: Phase 1 — high-value aisles (power tools, appliances) across all 200 stores; Phase 2 — full store coverage; integrate with replenishment system per W4 for automated restock order generation
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / COO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 6–12 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1569_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1569_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1569_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1569_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-331 (ensure controlled execution — Emerging Technology &amp; PoC (PA-30.1).) | - operational: IT Innovation Lead review and approval gate on alert thresholds
Owner: IT Innovation Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1569_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1569_Annotation12" targetRef="W1569_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
