    <bpmn:process id="W_W1570" name="W1570. In-Store Customer Navigation &amp; Wayfinding Mobile App PoC, Indoor Positioning &amp; Product Location Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or customer feedback indicating difficulty finding products in large-format stores; or ecommerce BOPIS pickup time optimization initiative
Frequency: PoC planning: quarterly; PoC execution: 3-month pilot; post-PoC evaluation: at completion
Volume: PoC scope: 5 pilot stores; target: customers using BuildRight mobile app for in-store navigation during pilot
Owner: IT Innovation Lead
Participants: IT Innovation Lead, Indoor Positioning Vendor, Ecommerce Manager, Store Manager (pilot stores), UX Designer, GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Source: workflow W1570 — In-Store Customer Navigation &amp; Wayfinding Mobile App PoC, Indoor Positioning &amp; Product Location Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1570_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1570_Lane1" name="IT Innovation Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1570_Lane2" name="Indoor Positioning Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1570_Lane3" name="Ecommerce Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1570_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1570_Start5" name="Annual innovation portfolio review per W690; or customer feedback indicating difficulty…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1570_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1570_Task6" name="PoC planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PoC planning: Evaluate indoor positioning technologies: (a) Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) beacons: install beacons throughout store at ~5-meter intervals; accuracy: 1–3 meters; cost: PHP 500–1,000/beacon × ~200 beacons/store = PHP 100–200K/store; (b) Wi-Fi fingerprinting: use existing store Wi-Fi access points; accuracy: 3–5 meters; lower hardware cost but lower accuracy; (c) select technology: BLE beacons for higher accuracy (recommendation); (d) pilot stores: 5 stores with varying layouts; (e) success criteria: (i) positioning accuracy ≤ 3 meters for 90% of readings, (ii) customer adoption: &gt; 10% of app users use navigation feature during pilot, (iii) customer satisfaction: &gt; 80% find the feature useful, (iv) reduction in &quot;where is...&quot; staff inquiries ≥ 20%
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1570_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1570_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1570_Task7" name="Store mapping &amp; beacon deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store mapping &amp; beacon deployment: (a) UX Designer creates detailed indoor map for each pilot store: (i) department boundaries, aisle layout, shelf positions, key landmarks (paint station, tool rental counter, customer service, restrooms), (ii) map linked to product location data from W29 (product → department → aisle → bay); (b) install BLE beacons in pilot stores: (i) mount beacons on ceiling at grid intervals, (ii) calibrate: walk store with reference device to map beacon signals to physical locations, (iii) verify accuracy with test walks; (c) integrate indoor positioning SDK into BuildRight mobile app
Responsible (R): Indoor Positioning Vendor / IT Innovation Lead / UX Designer
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 3–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1570_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1570_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1570_Task8" name="Feature development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Feature development: Ecommerce team develops in-store navigation feature: (a) product search with location result: &quot;PVC Pipe ½&quot; × 3m — Aisle 7, Bay 3, Shelf C — 35 meters from your location&quot;; (b) interactive store map with &quot;You are here&quot; blue dot; (c) turn-by-turn walking directions (visual arrows on map, not audio — store environment is noisy); (d) &quot;Find nearby&quot; suggestions for complementary products; (e) &quot;Navigate to BOPIS pickup&quot; shortcut; (f) analytics: track navigation usage, popular destinations, and customer paths
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Team / UX Designer
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 4–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1570_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1570_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1570_Task9" name="PoC execution (3 months)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: PoC execution (3 months): (a) promote the feature to customers entering pilot stores: &quot;Use the BuildRight app to find any product in our store! Look for the &#x27;Find in Store&#x27; button&quot;; (b) measure: (i) positioning accuracy (test walks weekly), (ii) feature usage (daily active users, navigation sessions, popular search terms), (iii) customer satisfaction (in-app survey after navigation use), (iv) &quot;where is...&quot; inquiry count reduction (Staff Associate tracking); (c) weekly: IT Innovation Lead reviews metrics and adjusts beacon calibration if accuracy degrades
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1570_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1570_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1570_Task10" name="Post-PoC evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-PoC evaluation: (a) technology assessment: positioning accuracy, reliability, maintenance requirements (beacon battery life: 2–3 years; calibration drift); (b) customer adoption and satisfaction; (c) chain-wide rollout cost: 200 stores × PHP 100–200K beacons + app development = PHP 20–40M + ongoing maintenance PHP 2–4M/year; (d) business case: staff time savings (fewer &quot;where is...&quot; inquiries) + customer experience improvement + BOPIS pickup time reduction; (e) recommend expand/discontinue
Responsible (R): IT Innovation Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1570_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1570_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1570_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1570_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1570_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-331 (ensure controlled execution — Emerging Technology &amp; PoC (PA-30.1).) | - operational: IT Innovation Lead review and approval gate
Owner: IT Innovation Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
